---
import StandardLayout from "../../layouts/StandardLayout.astro";
import IconCallout from "../../components/prototype/IconCallout.astro";
import "../../styles/prototype-callout.css";
---

<StandardLayout code="PROT" title="Callout & Formula Box – Design Prototype" framework="Design">
  <p class="text-supporting">
    <strong>Design prototype only.</strong> This page does not modify any existing
    callout, page, or stylesheet. It demonstrates a proposed treatment where a small
    Lucide icon interrupts the top border of each educational box instead of using an
    emoji inside the content. Colours, spacing, typography, and border thickness are
    unchanged from the current design.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pc-section-title">All box types, side by side</h2>

  <div class="pc-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="pc-cell-label">1 &middot; Information Box</div>
      <IconCallout variant="info">
        <strong style="font-weight:600">Qualitative characteristics in action:</strong>
        the lower-of-cost-and-NRV test balances relevance (reflecting a genuine decline
        in recoverable value) against faithful representation (never allowing inventory
        to be carried above what it can realistically generate).
      </IconCallout>
    </div>

    <div>
      <div class="pc-cell-label">2 &middot; Warning Box</div>
      <IconCallout variant="warn">
        <strong style="font-weight:600">A common exam trap:</strong> students sometimes
        try to net investment income against the general borrowing pool – the netting rule
        applies exclusively to specific, traceable borrowings, not the general facility.
      </IconCallout>
    </div>

    <div>
      <div class="pc-cell-label">3 &middot; Success Box</div>
      <IconCallout variant="suc">
        <strong style="font-weight:600">Correct application confirmed:</strong> when the
        construction-phase operating loss is incurred, it is recognised immediately in
        profit or loss and is not capitalised into the asset's carrying amount.
      </IconCallout>
    </div>

    <div>
      <div class="pc-cell-label">4 &middot; Danger Box</div>
      <IconCallout variant="danger">
        <strong style="font-weight:600">Never restate prior periods for an estimate
        change</strong> – even when the effect is material. Retrospectively "correcting"
        a genuine change in estimate would misrepresent the information available to
        management at the time.
      </IconCallout>
    </div>

    <div style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
      <div class="pc-cell-label">5 &middot; Formula / Key Concept Box</div>
      <IconCallout variant="formula">
        <div class="pc-formula-label">Depreciation charge (straight line)</div>
        <div class="pc-formula-eq">
          Annual depreciation = (Cost &minus; Residual value) &divide; Useful life
        </div>
        <p class="text-supporting" style="margin:6px 0 0;">
          Applied prospectively; a change in estimate (life or residual value) is never
          restated against prior periods under IAS 8.
        </p>
      </IconCallout>
    </div>
  </div>
</StandardLayout>


